  "answer": "This looks like the same problem as PowerToys#45452. There, Ctrl+W stopped working in every app while Command Palette was on, and it worked again once Command Palette was off. The cause was a leftover hotkey in Command Palette's settings. A command or extension had been assigned that hotkey, and it stayed after the extension was removed. To fix it, close Command Palette and open %localappdata%\\Packages\\Microsoft.CommandPalette_8wekyb3d8bbwe\\LocalState\\settings.json. In the \"CommandHotkeys\" array, look for an entry with \"ctrl\": true and \"code\": 66, which is the B key. Delete that entry. The key is released as soon as the entry is gone. You can also check Command Palette's settings for any command that has Ctrl+B assigned and clear it there. If you find no such entry, upload a Report Bug zip and your settings.json to the ticket so it can be investigated further."
 },
